# SurfContext Documentation Site

The official documentation and specification site for SurfContext — the open standard
for agent-ready project documentation (ARDS v5.2). The site is a Rust/Axum server that
renders SurfDoc source through `surf-parse`; it is served at surfcontext.org.

This file is the canonical root context for this repository. The `## Core` section below
is the guaranteed-context head: `tools/surfcontext-sync.sh` extracts it byte-for-byte and
injects a stamped copy into the root files each harness auto-loads. Edit the rules here
and re-run the sync; never edit a generated block.

## Core

### Absolute rules

1. **Git & deploy** — never run `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, or any deploy
   command; never amend, rebase, or force-push. Work stays in the working tree and the
   repository owner runs the commands.
2. **Attribution** — never add an AI co-author trailer or any other AI-assistant
   attribution to commits, code, docs, or files. The repository owner is the sole author.
3. **Verification** — verify every remembered fact against the live source before acting
   on it: read the file, run the command, fetch the page. When memory and the source
   disagree, the source wins, and the stale memory is corrected in the same pass.
4. **Source of truth** — `CONTEXT.surf` plus the canonical tree named in
   `surfcontext.json` are the single source of truth. `SPEC.surf` is the specification;
   the `/spec` page is a rendered view of it and is never hand-authored.
5. **Format** — all documentation in this repository is SurfDoc (`.surf`). `README.md`
   stays Markdown by GitHub convention (SPEC Section 3, Exceptions).
6. **No third-party framing** — never describe SurfContext, SurfDoc or ARDS as based on,
   like, or inspired by another company's product. Harness file names the standard must
   name (`CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.cursorrules`, `copilot-instructions.md`) are file
   names, not comparisons.

### The one rule that is easy to get wrong

The `/spec` route renders `SPEC.surf` directly. There is no hand-written spec page any
more — `content/spec.html` was deleted precisely because it drifted to ARDS v3.0 while the
ratified spec moved on. Amend `SPEC.surf` and the site follows.

## Key Files

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `SPEC.surf` | The ARDS specification — canonical text, rendered by `/spec` |
| `src/main.rs` | Axum server, routes, static and asset mounts |
| `src/routes/landing.rs` | `/` — renders `content/landing.surf` |
| `src/routes/spec.rs` | `/spec` — renders `SPEC.surf` through `surf-parse` |
| `src/routes/getting_started.rs` | `/getting-started` — serves `content/getting_started.html` |
| `src/routes/tools.rs` | `/tools` — renders `content/tools.surf` |
| `src/routes/whats_new.rs` | `/whats-new` — renders `content/whats_new.surf` |
| `src/routes/download.rs` | `POST /api/download` — builds the starter-kit zip in memory |
| `src/routes/talks.rs` | `/talks` lists the decks; `/talks/{slug}` serves one full-screen via surf-parse `to_slides_html` |
| `src/html.rs` | Base page shell: head, nav, footer, theme bootstrap |
| `content/*.surf` | Page source for every route except getting-started |
| `content/talks/*.surf` | Slide decks (`::deck` / `::slide`), one per talk, registered in `TALKS` |
| `tools/ards-lint.py` | Conformance and drift linter (the CI gate) |
| `tools/surfcontext-sync.sh` | Reference sync — Core injection into harness root files |
| `tools/ards-tests.sh` | Tools battery; must stay green |
| `templates/`, `playbooks/` | Starter templates and executable playbooks |
| `surfcontext.json` | ARDS manifest (dogfooding) |

## Architecture

A single Rust binary. Each route is a module under `src/routes/` that parses SurfDoc
source with `surf-parse` and wraps the rendered fragment in the shared shell from
`src/html.rs`. No database, no authentication, no build step for content — the `.surf`
files are compiled into the binary with `include_str!`, so a content change is a rebuild.

```
SPEC.surf          --> /spec        (surf-parse)
content/*.surf     --> /, /tools, /whats-new  (surf-parse)
content/*.html     --> /getting-started       (served as-is)
content/talks/     --> /talks/{slug}          (surf-parse slides)
src/routes/        --> route modules
src/html.rs        --> page shell
static/, assets/   --> mounted directories
```

## Stack & Development

**Stack**: Rust (edition 2024), Axum 0.8, Tokio, tower-http, surf-parse 0.5.1
**Build**: `cargo build --locked`
**Test**: `cargo test --locked`
**Tools battery**: `bash tools/ards-tests.sh`
**Lint**: `python3 tools/ards-lint.py`
**Run locally**: `cargo run` (listens on `PORT`, default 3000)
**Deploy**: Fly.io — `fly.production.toml`, `fly.staging.toml`, `fly.develop.toml`

## Conventions

- Dark-first theming with a light toggle, persisted in `localStorage`
- All page content is SurfDoc where a route renders it
- No heavy images, no external runtime dependencies
- Mobile responsive

## Active Work

- **ARDS v5.2 ratified** in `SPEC.surf` — SurfDoc-native context (Section 45)
- **`/spec` repointed** from the deleted `content/spec.html` to `SPEC.surf`
- **D-SC-1 closed** — `README.md` is a five-line pointer to `README.surf`, `CONTEXT.surf`
  and `SPEC.surf`; the GitHub landing view reads acceptably. Verified, no change made
- **D-SC-2 closed** — the unserved Next.js remnant is retired: `app/`, `components/` and
  `tests/` (17 files) plus the eight root JS/TS configs are deleted. The Dockerfile only
  ever copied the Cargo manifests, `src/`, `content/`, `static/` and `assets/`, and CI runs
  `cargo` only, so nothing served changes
- **D-SC-3 closed in the parser's favour** — `surf-parse` 0.19.1 adds `specification` to the
  front matter type vocabulary additively; `SPEC.surf`'s declared type is unchanged. The
  route test is now a zero-error pin instead of a tolerated-defect pin
- **Open (D-SC-4, new)** — closing D-SC-3 uncovered what the old single-error pin was
  masking: `SPEC.surf` declares `version: 5.2`, but `FrontMatter::version` is an integer, so
  the whole front matter block is still discarded — now as a P005 *warning*, not an error.
  `SPEC.surf` is a byte-identical mirror of canon and not ours to edit, so this needs a
  ruling: widen the parser's `version` field to accept a decimal, or amend canon. Pinned by
  `spec_surf_residual_is_only_the_decimal_version_warning`
- **Open (ship order)** — `Cargo.toml` no longer requests the `axum` feature and the
  stylesheet handler moved into `src/main.rs`; the git dependency must be repinned
  (`cargo update -p surf-parse`) once `surf-parse` v0.19.1 is tagged and pushed
